{"title":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","category":"Engineering","bank":"nta_abhyas_jee_main","subject":"Physics","chapter":"Mathematics in Physics","count":2,"questions":[{"id":93690,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Mathematics in Physics","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"The resultant of two vectors is perpendicular to first vector of magnitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. If the resultant has magnitude <math><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mtext> N</mtext></math>, then magnitude of second vector is","options":["<math><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> N</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>","<math><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> N</mi></math>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fnta_abhyas%252Fjee_main%252Fimages%252Fzmthevymlndgmxnrohxtnijnnvhfngvzhikpyhkkurmkjqybza.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fnta_abhyas%2Fjee_main%2Fimages%2Fzmthevymlndgmxnrohxtnijnnvhfngvzhikpyhkkurmkjqybza.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fnta_abhyas%2Fjee_main%2Fimages%2Fzmthevymlndgmxnrohxtnijnnvhfngvzhikpyhkkurmkjqybza.png?alt=media\" /><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B Cos θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B Sin</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mtext>B</mtext><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e863e4404ffefabf652c"},{"id":93691,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Mathematics in Physics","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"Two forces <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> whose magnitude are in the ratio <math><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> give a resultant of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>28</mn><mo> </mo><mtext>N</mtext></math>. If the angle of their inclination is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></msup><mo>,</mo></math> then the magnitude of force <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> will be ----- <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.","options":[],"answer":"20.00","solution":"Let <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> be the two forces.<br /><br />Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>;</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>28</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>°</mo></mrow></msup></math> .<br /><br />We know that <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>°</mo></mrow></msup></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>9</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>28</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br />Hence, force <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20 </mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mtext>N</mtext></math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e86303ec189ffa9eafc7","correctValue":"20.00","questionType":"numerical","type":"numerical"}]}